"channels. Participants in DMs/GMs can also enable or disable calls."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/configure/plugins-configuration-settings.rst:356
msgid ""
"**false**: Only system admins can enable or disable calls on specific "
"channels."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/configure/plugins-configuration-settings.rst:356
msgid ""
"``config.json`` setting: ``PluginSettings`` > ``Plugins`` > "
"``com.mattermost.calls`` > ``allowenablecalls``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/configure/plugins-configuration-settings.rst:357
msgid "Environment variable: ``MM_CALLS_ALLOW_ENABLE_CALLS``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/configure/plugins-configuration-settings.rst:368
msgid "Test mode"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/configure/plugins-configuration-settings.rst:370
msgid ""
"*This setting was called Enable on all channels until Mattermost v7.7. It"
" was renamed to defaultenabled in code and Test Mode in-product and is "
"only applicable to self-hosted deployments.*"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/configure/plugins-configuration-settings.rst:373
msgid ""
"**false**: Test mode is enabled and only system admins can start calls in"
" channels."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/configure/plugins-configuration-settings.rst:374
msgid ""
"**true**: Live mode is enabled and all team members can start calls in "
"channels."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/configure/plugins-configuration-settings.rst:374
msgid ""
"``config.json`` setting: ``PluginSettings`` > ``Plugins`` > "
"``com.mattermost.calls`` > ``defaultenabled``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/configure/plugins-configuration-settings.rst:375
msgid "Environment variable: ``MM_CALLS_DEFAULT_ENABLED``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/configure/plugins-configuration-settings.rst:379
msgid ""
"Use this setting as a system admin to confirm calls work as expected. "
"When **false**, users attempting to start calls are prompted to contact a"
" system admin, and system admins are prompted to confirm that calls are "
"working as expected before switching to live mode."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/configure/plugins-configuration-settings.rst:389
msgid "ICE host override"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/configure/plugins-configuration-settings.rst:392
msgid ""
"This setting can be used to override the host addresses that get "
"advertised to clients when connecting to calls. The accepted formats are "
"the following:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/configure/plugins-configuration-settings.rst:396
msgid "A single IP address (e.g. ``10.0.0.1``)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/configure/plugins-configuration-settings.rst:397
msgid "A single hostname or FQDN (e.g. ``calls.myserver.tld``)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/configure/plugins-configuration-settings.rst:398
msgid ""
"(starting in v0.17.0) A comma separated list of externalAddr/internalAddr"
" mappings (e.g. ``10.0.0.1/172.0.0.1,10.0.0.2/172.0.0.2``)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/configure/plugins-configuration-settings.rst:400
#: ../../source/administration-guide/configure/plugins-configuration-settings.rst:453
msgid ""
"This is an optional field. Changing this setting requires a plugin "
"restart to take effect."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/configure/plugins-configuration-settings.rst:393
msgid ""
"``config.json`` setting:  ``PluginSettings`` > ``Plugins`` > "
"``com.mattermost.calls`` > ``icehostoverride``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/configure/plugins-configuration-settings.rst:394
msgid "Environment variable: ``MM_CALLS_ICE_HOST_OVERRIDE``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/configure/plugins-configuration-settings.rst:405
msgid ""
"Depending on the network infrastructure (e.g. instance behind a NAT "
"device) it may be necessary to set this field to the client facing "
"external IP for clients to connect. When empty or unset, the RTC service "
"will attempt to find the instance's public IP through STUN."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/configure/plugins-configuration-settings.rst:406
msgid ""
"A hostname (e.g. domain name) can be specified in this setting, but an IP"
" address will be passed to clients. This means that a DNS resolution "
"happens on the Mattermost instance which could result in a different IP "
"address from the one the clients would see, causing connectivity to fail."
" When in doubt, we recommend using an IP address directly or confirming "
"that the resolution on the host side reflects the one on the client."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/configure/plugins-configuration-settings.rst:418
msgid "ICE host port override"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/configure/plugins-configuration-settings.rst:421
msgid ""
"This setting can be used to override the port used in the ICE host "
"candidates that get advertised to clients when connecting to calls."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/configure/plugins-configuration-settings.rst:425
msgid ""
"This can be useful in case there are additional network components (e.g. "
"NLBs) in front of the RTC server that may route the calls traffic through"
" a different port. Changing this setting requires a plugin restart to "
"take effect."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/configure/plugins-configuration-settings.rst:422
msgid ""
"``config.json`` setting: ``PluginSettings`` > ``Plugins`` > "
"``com.mattermost.calls`` > ``icehostportoverride``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/configure/plugins-configuration-settings.rst:423
msgid "Environment variable: ``MM_CALLS_ICE_HOST_PORT_OVERRIDE``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/configure/plugins-configuration-settings.rst:430
#: ../../source/administration-guide/configure/plugins-configuration-settings.rst:457
